# H-lane progress log — homology generation for PeriodGeneratingLoops

2026-06-11 session start. Branch feat/homology-generation @ origin/main (90c1da7).
Goal: attack `PeriodGeneratingLoops` via `of_homology_span` — produce 2g analytic
loops whose `loopToHomology` classes ℤ-generate every loop's class, WITHOUT
AX_PeriodCycleBasis in the kernel closure.

Statement-chain analysis (initial):
- Target: ∃ γs : Fin (2*genus X) → AnalyticLoop X x₀,
    ∀ δ, loopToHomology δ ∈ span ℤ (range (loopToHomology ∘ γs)).
- Key insight 1 (no smoothing needed): the loop classes form an AddSubgroup of
  H1 (trans/reverse/refl of analytic loops are analytic — ArcAlgebra has
  arc-level trans/reverse; constant arc generalizes Line/Witnesses.constLoop).
  So the span A := span ℤ (range loopToHomology) EQUALS the set of loop classes,
  and any generating set extracted from A consists of analytic-loop classes
  automatically.
- Key insight 2 (Noetherian extraction): if H1 X x₀ is a f.g. ℤ-module, A is
  f.g. (ℤ Noetherian), and its generators are loop classes ⇒ Fin n version of
  the hypothesis, pure module theory.
- Key insight 3 (n vs 2g): n > 2g does NOT give discreteness (ℤ+ℤ√2 dense in ℝ:
  a f.g. subgroup of ℝ^N ℝ-spanning with > N generators can be dense). The
  count ≤ 2g is where the genus comparison (rank H1 ≤ 2·g_analytic) enters —
  genus X here is ANALYTIC genus (finrank ℂ HolomorphicOneForm). Note only ≤ is
  needed; ≥ comes free from B-3 ℝ-spanning.
- Reduction of n→2g: A ⊆ H1 free f.g. (Submodule.basisOfPid over PID ℤ) given
  [Module.Free ℤ H1] + [Module.Finite ℤ H1]; basis of A has card ≤ finrank H1
  ≤ 2g; basis elements ARE loop classes (insight 1); pad with constant loops.
- Mathlib FG inventory: NO finite-generation results for FundamentalGroup of
  compact spaces/manifolds at pin (no Group.FG near AlgebraicTopology or
  Topology/Homotopy). π₁-f.g.-of-compact-manifold must be built or named.

Planned bricks in Jacobians/RiemannSurface/HomologyGeneration.lean:
A. AnalyticLoop.trans/reverse/refl + loopToHomology hom lemmas
B. loopClasses AddSubgroup; span range loopToHomology = range loopToHomology
C. [Module.Finite ℤ (H1 X x₀)] ⇒ ∃ n γs, homology span (Fin n)
D. + [Module.Free] + finrank ≤ 2g ⇒ Fin (2g) version (basisOfPid + padding)
E. wiring: ⇒ PeriodGeneratingLoops ⇒ DiscreteTopology (loopPeriodLattice),
   axiom-free; kernel check NO AX_PeriodCycleBasis.

